    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n40927" root="هجد" body-key="h">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَاجِدٌ</span></b>  <i>Sleeping:</i> (T, L, Msb:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُجُودٌ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُجَّدٌ</span>. (Msb.) [See an ex. in a verse cited voce
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُرِمٌّ</span>, in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رم</span>.] ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also, (L,) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هَجُودٌ</span></b>  (L,
K) and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُتَهَجِّدٌ</span></b>  (T, L) <i>Praying in the night:</i>
(T, L, K:) pl. of the first, (L,) or second, (L,
K,) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُجُودٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُجَّدٌ</span>. (L, K.) <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُجْدٌ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هُجَّدٌ</span>
are also fem. pls. [app. in both of the above
senses]. (A.)

